 "builderFixesThisFoundNote": "Resolving these three sources exposed that CoursePresets cloned every declared SubPart from the source on top of the root clone's own subtree, so any nested assembly was built twice: the pilot's pistons carried a duplicate spring and head, and a mace would have carried a duplicate ten-part chain. Sub-parts are now resolved inside the root clone first. Part counts fell from 156 to 143 (Ball Barrage) and 151 to 142 (Whirlpool Waltz); both spec hashes changed as a result."
